From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 13:29:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: tests: WED end to end, against a fake of the
 Ethernet side

The MilkFlint WED setting (mt7915e wed_enable) puts the router's Wi-Fi
on these paths, and most of them had no test: the WED attach at probe,
its reset handshake, WED's rx buffers, the rings it takes over, the flow
offload path, the WO's station records and rx counters.

tests/wed-fake.h models the Ethernet driver's WED (mtk_wed.c) as the
driver sees it: attach drops the RCU lock and hands over the WED's DMA
device and interrupt, detach clears the device, ring setups give their
rings registers in the WED's own register file, the rest is counted. It
can be registered where mtk_wed_device_attach() looks.

- mt76-wed: rx buffer fill and release (both bands' pools, running out
  of rx tokens releases everything), ring setup per queue type, the DMA
  reset handshake, TC offload, WED token counting, tx status ids.
- mt7915-mmio: WED init with no WED, a refusing one, an attaching one
  (interrupt, DMA device, 32-bit mask) and one that can't do 32-bit DMA;
  the L1 reset under RTNL; WO rx counters; the interrupt mask through WED.
- mt7915-mac: the tx buffers WED sends from.
- mt7915-main: station records to the WO (a refused one isn't sent), WDS
  wcids, four-address mode, the forward path.
- mt7915-dma: the MT7986's rings with a WED attached, through a reset and
  the teardown.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
